{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-7729"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Community Household Goods Rental Operations"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "7729"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :commercial/household-goods-rental-services
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:consumer-protection :shared-asset-access :financial-inclusion]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :household-rental-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :labor]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:optimization]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "HouseholdRentalAdvisor ⊣ Household Rental Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph (langgraph.graph, householdrentalops.operation/build),
 append-only audit ledger (householdrentalops.store/ledger +
 append-ledger!, MemStore and a DatomicStore backed by langchain.db via
 langchain-store.core). A genuinely compiled StateGraph (`:intake ->
 :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval ->
 :commit / :hold`) with `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` +
 in-memory checkpointer for real human-in-the-loop resume. A
 back-office OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for community household-
 goods rent-to-own (furniture/appliances/consumer-electronics) -- not
 direct disclosure-scope compliance-verification authority and not
 condition-check override/waiver authority (both permanently blocked
 ops, human/compliance-officer exclusive). Five ops
 (`:release-rental-agreement` / `:dispatch-delivery-inspection-mission`
 / `:dispatch-pickup-inspection-mission` / `:log-reconciliation-record`
 / `:flag-disclosure-concern`), all `:effect :propose` only. Seven HARD
 invariants elaborate this blueprint's Governor, all traceable to this
 repo's own pre-existing README.md/docs (never a newly-fabricated
 regulatory claim): disclosure-scope-unverified (applies to every op --
 'agreements cannot be released outside verified disclosure scope'),
 no-execution, decision-authority-blocked (disclosure-scope-
 verification finalization / condition-check override), op-not-allowed,
 tco-disclosure-missing (`:release-rental-agreement` without a confirmed
 `:tco-disclosed?` -- 'total-cost-of-ownership-disclosure management'),
 condition-check-incomplete (delivery/pickup mission without a completed
 `:condition-check-completed?` -- 'a delivery/pickup without a completed
 condition check'), and reconciliation-evidence-missing
 (`:log-reconciliation-record` without non-empty `:evidence` --
 'reconciliation records require verified evidence'), all quoting this
 repo's own docs/business-model.md Trust Controls and docs/operator-
 guide.md Minimum Production Controls verbatim rather than citing a new
 external standard. `:flag-disclosure-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a
 human compliance officer via the compiled graph's `:request-approval`
 node (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume, proven by
 `test/householdrentalops/operation_test.cljc` exercising commit /
 hard-hold (unverified scope) / hard-hold (incomplete condition check) /
 escalate-approve / escalate-reject / phase-0-forces-escalation /
 reconciliation-record commit and hard-hold through the REAL compiled
 graph end to end, plus a `clojure -M:dev:run` demo runner producing
 real ledger entries for five scenarios). MemStore and DatomicStore pass
 the same store-contract test
 (`test/householdrentalops/store_contract_test.cljc`). 42 tests / 150
 assertions green (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors/0
 warnings, demo runnable end-to-end against both Store backends
 (`clojure -M:dev:run`). Governance-doc set and `docs/` were already
 present (README.md/business-model.md/operator-guide.md fully specify
 the rental-purchase-agreement/disclosure-scope, TCO-disclosure,
 robotics delivery/pickup condition-inspection and reconciliation-
 record scope this implementation covers); `src/`, `test/`, `deps.edn`
 and CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, sibling-checkout pattern for
 :local/root deps, mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0115/cloud-itonami-isic-869)
 were the gaps this fix closes."}
